    detail: >-
      Five finders, three candidates, adversarial verification confirming two. (1) push_code_point
      discards the hex digits take_radix already consumed when the code point is not a character
      (a UTF-16 surrogate \uD800, a \U above 0x10FFFF), emitting only the two-byte marker - a
      silent divergence from the module's own claim that an escape bash does not know stays
      literal; verified by tokenizing both shapes and comparing with a real bash, which keeps the
      six-byte literal. Important, not blocker: Chrome never emits a surrogate escape. (2)
      Command.saw_data_flag is redundant with !data.is_empty(), since -d '' still pushes an empty
      element - nit. Refuted: UC-6 quoting two example refusal wordings and the format refusal
      string is stating a wire-visible contract the same file already does for the import
      envelope, not copying code; the verifier did note the doc/v1 note's self-description
      ("not their wording") is imprecise, carried forward as a note correction in round 2.
